-- CHAOS-DRILL-CALIBRATION-1 (2026-10-26, pillar autonomy and security; agent_issues 100482, 1000057, 1000214)
--
-- WHAT WAS MEASURED (qnfo-audit SELECT only, 2026-10-26 07:00-07:45Z, then re-measured by an independent reviewer who found three majors in the first version of this file)
--   CHAOS-DRILL-1 files CHAOS-DRILL-FAILED-1 when a control's alternate shows no evidence at its 6-hourly drill and closes the issue itself on the next pass. Nine were open and all nine drills
--   were failing at 07:01Z. Three are calibration defects of the probe, one is a control the register cannot honestly certify:
--   1. ops-jobs-payload-redaction (issue 100482, critical, 111 hours): the probe greps ops_jobs.payload for the phrases one-time code, verification code and the like. Six rows match, all
--      origin budget-promote, status succeeded, 150 to 390 KB, and json_each over $.messages puts every hit in a role tool message (repository files, a CLI document, test text), none in a
--      user or system message, no digit follows a phrase. BUT a budget-promote payload is the owner's whole interactive transcript: redactJobBody keeps user and system messages verbatim
--      (qnfo-ops/log-redact.test.mjs), so a link or code the owner types and later promotes would be stored in clear and a probe that skips the origin would never look. The first version
--      of this file skipped the origin and was refuted by a reproduction. Now: every other origin is scanned whole, a budget-promote row is scanned in its user and system messages only
--      (251 user and 69 system messages on live, zero hits). The 15-day sweep check is unchanged.
--   2. research-floor-rearm (issue 1000057): the probe demanded the table bak_20261019_research_parked and a park-rearm-tick event within 48 hours. The table was the frozen input of the one-shot
--      step floorRearmTick (34 rows re-armed on 2026-10-19) and is gone (no automated dropper exists in the repository, 16 bak tables exist, the oldest from 2026-10-24), so floorRearmTick has
--      been a silent no-op since FLOOR-REARM-NOOP-1. park-rearm-tick is logged only when a row was re-armed (qnfo-research-exec/worker.js, about line 31012), so it is no heartbeat and the probe
--      would fail again whenever nothing is left to re-arm. The sweep runs in the hourly minute-0 branch that also logs idea-to-publish every hour: the probe now reads that (180 minutes, the
--      120-minute rule plus the cadence), keeps the park_rearm lever check, and the register location no longer names the missing table. The follow-up (an unconditional heartbeat from the
--      sweep and the fate of floorRearmTick) is filed at the end of this file as PARK-REARM-HEARTBEAT-1.
--   3. evolve-wip-recovery (issue 1000214) had an alternate and no probe. The probe reads code tasks merged in 24 hours by merged_at (17 on 2026-10-26, against 21 by the re-stamped
--      updated_at). It is liveness evidence that the planner drains, and its window note says so.
--   4. research-quality-gate (critical path, issue 1000214): NO probe. Its alternate, the structural sweep that quarantines after publication, was removed by PUB-GATE-NO-WITHDRAW-1 today (failing
--      papers become revise), and its register evidence says the source-side prevention issue 1000209 and a live quarantine probe stay open until independently verified. A probe on a daily
--      snapshot would stamp alternate_tested_at on a control nobody has verified. The register's own sanctioned state is used instead: ALTERNATE-NOT-EXERCISABLE in the evidence, so
--      v_control_alternate_status reads not-exercisable and the control leaves the no-probe count without a false tested stamp.
--   Not touched on purpose: the other five drills (qnfo-research-exec single executor, research-revise-refs-extend, remediation reopen on relapse, idea-triaged-hold-owner-and-reentry,
--   compat-advance-review-gate) fail on real missing evidence in code other sessions hold, and agent-ws-reactivation-prerequisites waits on a task the code loop marked needs_human.
--
-- Effect: the 13:01Z drill reads ok for ops-jobs-payload-redaction and research-floor-rearm and closes 100482 and 1000057 itself, and 1000214 closes once its register check reads 0.
-- The old probe texts are kept as disabled rows named <control>@before-calibration-1 (not in a bak_ table, which the fleet purges), and the Rollback line restores from them.
-- Edited probes are guarded so a second apply, or a probe someone has since changed, is left alone. No trigger, no cron, no DROP.
--
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: UPDATE control_alternate_probes SET probe_sql = (SELECT h.probe_sql FROM control_alternate_probes h WHERE h.control = control_alternate_probes.control || '@before-calibration-1'), window_note = (SELECT h.window_note FROM control_alternate_probes h WHERE h.control = control_alternate_probes.control || '@before-calibration-1') WHERE control IN ('ops-jobs-payload-redaction', 'research-floor-rearm') AND EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM control_alternate_probes h WHERE h.control = control_alternate_probes.control || '@before-calibration-1'); DELETE FROM control_alternate_probes WHERE control = 'evolve-wip-recovery' AND last_run_at IS NULL; UPDATE control_registry SET evidence = replace(evidence, ' ALTERNATE-NOT-EXERCISABLE: the registered alternate, the qnfo-cloud-ops structural sweep that quarantines after publication, was removed by PUB-GATE-NO-WITHDRAW-1 on 2026-10-26 (failing papers become revise and notes.quarantined is always 0), so no quarantine path exists to exercise. The hourly sweep leaves cloud_ops_events kind quality-score as its heartbeat. The source-side prevention issue 1000209 and a live paper-quarantine probe stay open until independently verified. Recorded by CHAOS-DRILL-CALIBRATION-1.', '') WHERE control = 'research-quality-gate'; UPDATE control_registry SET location = 'qnfo-research-exec floorRearmTick (FLOOR-REARM-1), hourly sweep' || char(59) || ' bak_20261019_research_parked' WHERE control = 'research-floor-rearm' AND location = 'qnfo-research-exec parkRearmTick (hourly sweep, minute-0 branch) and floorRearmTick (FLOOR-REARM-1, a one-shot list of 2026-10-19 that is exhausted and no longer exists, so the step is a silent no-op, FLOOR-REARM-NOOP-1)'

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO control_alternate_probes (control, probe_sql, window_note, enabled)
SELECT control || '@before-calibration-1', probe_sql, COALESCE(window_note, ''), 0 FROM control_alternate_probes WHERE control IN ('ops-jobs-payload-redaction', 'research-floor-rearm');

UPDATE control_alternate_probes SET probe_sql = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ops_jobs WHERE (COALESCE(origin, '''') <> ''budget-promote'' OR NOT json_valid(payload)) AND (payload LIKE ''%magic-link%'' OR payload LIKE ''%magic_link%'' OR payload LIKE ''%/login%token=%'' OR payload LIKE ''%/verify%token=%'' OR payload LIKE ''%/reset%token=%'' OR payload LIKE ''%verification code%'' OR payload LIKE ''%one-time code%'' OR payload LIKE ''%login code%'')) THEN ''a stored ops_jobs payload still holds a login link or a one-time code'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ops_jobs j, json_each(CASE WHEN json_valid(j.payload) THEN j.payload ELSE ''{}'' END, ''$.messages'') m WHERE j.origin = ''budget-promote'' AND json_extract(m.value, ''$.role'') IN (''user'', ''system'') AND (json_extract(m.value, ''$.content'') LIKE ''%magic-link%'' OR json_extract(m.value, ''$.content'') LIKE ''%magic_link%'' OR json_extract(m.value, ''$.content'') LIKE ''%/login%token=%'' OR json_extract(m.value, ''$.content'') LIKE ''%/verify%token=%'' OR json_extract(m.value, ''$.content'') LIKE ''%/reset%token=%'' OR json_extract(m.value, ''$.content'') LIKE ''%verification code%'' OR json_extract(m.value, ''$.content'') LIKE ''%one-time code%'' OR json_extract(m.value, ''$.content'') LIKE ''%login code%'')) THEN ''a stored ops_jobs payload still holds a login link or a one-time code'' WHEN EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM ops_jobs WHERE status IN (''succeeded'', ''failed'', ''terminated'', ''cancelled'') AND updated_at < strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ'', ''now'', ''-15 days'')) THEN ''a terminal ops_jobs row is older than 15 days, so the 14-day sweep is not running'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed', window_note = 'state probe on the stored payloads and the 14-day sweep that bounds what a user-typed link can keep. A budget-promote payload is the owner interactive transcript: its user and system messages are kept verbatim by redactJobBody and are scanned here, while its tool messages (repository files, CLI help, test text that mention the phrases) are not: the six false positives of 2026-10-26 were all role tool. Every other origin, and a budget-promote payload that is not valid JSON, is scanned whole'
WHERE control = 'ops-jobs-payload-redaction' AND probe_sql LIKE '%one-time code%' AND probe_sql NOT LIKE '%json_each%';

UPDATE control_alternate_probes SET probe_sql = 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN COALESCE((SELECT value FROM ops_config WHERE key = ''park_rearm''), ''on'') NOT IN (''on'', ''off'') THEN ''ops_config park_rearm holds a value the sweep does not read, so its off lever is unreadable'' WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM cloud_ops_events WHERE kind = ''idea-to-publish'' AND ts > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-180 minutes'')) THEN ''no idea-to-publish event in 180 minutes, so the hourly minute-0 branch of qnfo-research-exec that runs the park re-arm sweep is not running'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed', window_note = '180 minutes: the hourly minute-0 branch of qnfo-research-exec logs idea-to-publish every hour (48 events in the last 48 hours on 2026-10-26) and runs the park re-arm sweep in the same branch. park-rearm-tick is not a heartbeat (it is logged only when a row was re-armed), so it is not used. The backup table bak_20261019_research_parked is no longer demanded: it was the frozen input of a one-shot step and is gone'
WHERE control = 'research-floor-rearm' AND probe_sql LIKE '%bak_20261019_research_parked%';

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO control_alternate_probes (control, probe_sql, window_note, enabled) VALUES
 ('evolve-wip-recovery', 'SELECT ''ok'' AS expected, CASE WHEN NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM code_tasks WHERE status = ''merged'' AND merged_at > strftime(''%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'', ''now'', ''-24 hours'')) THEN ''the code planner merged no task in 24 hours, so the planner that stands in for evolve-wip-recovery is not draining'' ELSE ''ok'' END AS observed', '24 h: the code planner merges tasks on its own. Liveness evidence by merged_at (17 tasks merged in the 24 hours to 2026-10-26 07:20Z), which bookkeeping does not re-stamp, not by updated_at. It shows the planner drains, not that recovery is off', 1);

UPDATE control_registry SET evidence = COALESCE(evidence, '') || ' ALTERNATE-NOT-EXERCISABLE: the registered alternate, the qnfo-cloud-ops structural sweep that quarantines after publication, was removed by PUB-GATE-NO-WITHDRAW-1 on 2026-10-26 (failing papers become revise and notes.quarantined is always 0), so no quarantine path exists to exercise. The hourly sweep leaves cloud_ops_events kind quality-score as its heartbeat. The source-side prevention issue 1000209 and a live paper-quarantine probe stay open until independently verified. Recorded by CHAOS-DRILL-CALIBRATION-1.'
WHERE control = 'research-quality-gate' AND COALESCE(evidence, '') NOT LIKE '%ALTERNATE-NOT-EXERCISABLE%';

UPDATE control_registry SET location = 'qnfo-research-exec parkRearmTick (hourly sweep, minute-0 branch) and floorRearmTick (FLOOR-REARM-1, a one-shot list of 2026-10-19 that is exhausted and no longer exists, so the step is a silent no-op, FLOOR-REARM-NOOP-1)'
WHERE control = 'research-floor-rearm' AND location LIKE '%bak_20261019_research_parked%';

INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT
  'PARK-REARM-HEARTBEAT-1: parkRearmTick logs only when it re-armed a row, so the sweep has no heartbeat, and floorRearmTick has been a silent no-op since its frozen list vanished',
  'Charter pillar: autonomy. CHAOS-DRILL-CALIBRATION-1 (2026-10-26): qnfo-research-exec logs park-rearm-tick only when a row was re-armed (about line 31012), so a healthy sweep with nothing left to re-arm is indistinguishable from a dead one: 13 of the last 48 hours had a tick, the gap since 2026-10-26T03:01Z is 14 hours at worst, and 585 PARKED-LOW-VALUE-1 rows are parked but the only kind it selects (REVIEW-UNRESOLVED-PARK-1) has none. The drill probe of research-floor-rearm now reads the hourly idea-to-publish event of the same branch instead. Also: floorRearmTick read the frozen list bak_20261019_research_parked (34 rows re-armed on 2026-10-19), the table is gone, and FLOOR-REARM-NOOP-1 turned its absence into a silent no-op. Fix: log an unconditional park-rearm-heartbeat event from parkRearmTick every hour with the counts, and retire floorRearmTick (or give it a list that is not a bak_ table) and update control_registry.location. Definition of done: the marker park-rearm-heartbeat is on main in qnfo-research-exec/worker.js.' || char(10) ||
  'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-research-exec/worker.js' || char(10) ||
  'code-anchor: if (_rearm.rearmed) await logEvent(env, "park-rearm-tick"' || char(10) ||
  'code-probe: {"paths": ["qnfo-research-exec/worker.js"], "contains": "park-rearm-heartbeat"}',
  'session', 'autonomy', 'medium', 'open',
  CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000,
  CAST(strftime('%s', 'now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE title LIKE 'PARK-REARM-HEARTBEAT-1:%');

